 "topics": [
  {
   "topic": "Handling a secret-echoing service response in NodeExecution, Run, and EffectAttempt",
   "members": [
    "r1.00",
    "r2.00",
    "r3.00"
   ],
   "runs": [
    1,
    2,
    3
   ],
   "questions": [
    "When the kernel detects a credential or token verbatim in a service response body, what NodeExecution status and run consequence does it record, and, for an effectful operation, what outcome does the EffectAttempt record?",
    "When a service response body is withheld for echoing a secret, what NodeExecution status and bounded facts are recorded, does the run fail or continue, and—if the operation was effectful—what outcome is recorded for its EffectAttempt?",
    "When such a body is withheld, what facts and lifecycle result for the NodeExecution and Run—does the node fail, succeed without outputs in some cases, wait, or acquire another status—and, for an effectful operation, is its EffectAttempt outcome recorded independently?"
   ],
   "units": [
    "context"
   ],
   "id": "T1",
   "judgement": {
    "kind": "judged_before",
    "quotes": [],
    "later_state": null,
    "divergence": "",
    "why": "This asks the same question as P1 about the NodeExecution status, Run consequence, and EffectAttempt outcome for a secret-echoing service response, and the deciding later-state passages have not changed.",
    "precedent": {
     "id": "P1",
     "round": "round-42",
     "topic": "Execution and effect outcome when a secret-echoing response body is withheld",
     "kind": "answered_later",
     "quotes": [
      "5. The outcome of one attempt is decided in this order:\n\n   | what happened | `read` operation | any other operation (EffectAttempt M26) |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | nothing could be sent: name resolution, connection or TLS failed | `service_unreachable` | `service_unreachable`, attempt `not_sent` |\n   | request may have been sent, no valid final response received (timeout, reset, EOF, a malformed status line or headers, only `1xx`) | `service_unreachable` | `outcome_unknown`, attempt `unknown` |\n   | status 3xx or 5xx, whatever the body's size — reading stops at the ceiling | `service_unreachable` for 5xx, `operation_failed` for 3xx | `outcome_unknown`, attempt `unknown` |\n   | status 4xx, whatever the body's size — reading stops at the ceiling | `operation_refused` | `operation_refused`, attempt `not_applied` |\n   | status 2xx, the body echoes the credential (rule 7), outputs do not fit rule 3, the body exceeds `service_response_bytes_max`, an output value exceeds `stored_value_bytes_max` (A15 rule 4, per output port, never the whole body) or a file output the spool ceilings | `contract_violation` | `contract_violation`, attempt `applied` |\n   | status 2xx, outputs fit | `succeeded` | `succeeded`, attempt `applied` |",
      "5. A node is failed when its record's status is `contract_violation`,\n   `sandbox_violation`, `timeout`, `resource_exhausted`, `crashed`,\n   `operation_refused` or `operation_failed`; `service_unreachable` and\n   `outcome_unknown` are waits, not failures, and their dependants wait, until\n   the owner's resolution makes the element count as succeeded or failed\n   (A11 rule 3).",
      "A waiting element\n   can still execute, so M19's \"no node can run any more\" holds only when\n   nothing waits: when nothing can\n   execute and nothing waits, the run ends: `succeeded` when every node concluded\n   succeeded or `skipped_by_guard`; otherwise `failed`."
     ],
     "why": "State 2 specifies that a credential-echoing 2xx response produces `contract_violation`, records an effectful attempt as `applied`, and ultimately makes the run `failed` once no work or waits remain; its ordered table also determines the outcomes for non-2xx responses."
    },
    "verified": true,
    "blocking": false
   }
  },
  {
   "topic": "Whether owners may inspect SpooledFile bytes or only recorded facts",
